;;; A core search cut at its budget prints its core as the smallest — M1e2
;;; **W23**, register row `W23/core-search-cut` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; banked by S1e2.2.23 (2026-11-05) from the inventory of 2026-11-05's F2
;;; (`plans/m1e2_correctness/inventory_2026-11-05/findings/F2_core_cut.ein`).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Eight pairs of givens, `(xi k)` and `(yi k)`, each lifted to `(pi k)` by
;;; either. `mk-a` concludes `(A k)` from `(p1 k) … (p8 k)`, so `(A k)` has
;;; 2^8 = 256 environments of eight facts, each `pi` from `xi` or `yi`.
;;; `mk-b` concludes `(B k)` from `(y1 k) … (y8 k)` alone, and `clash`
;;; concludes `(false)` from `(A k) (B k)`. Root is dead: no candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; R is empty, every node dead. The smallest set of givens from which the
;;; rules derive `(false)` is the eight `y` facts: they give `(B k)`, and
;;; every `(pi k)` through `(yi k)`, so `(A k)` too.
;;; `core-search-cut-control.ein`, the eight `y` facts alone, derives it.
;;;
;;; The core search keeps 64 environments per fact (`ExplanationBudget`),
;;; smallest first, and `(A k)`'s 256 are all of size 8, so which 64 it keeps
;;; is the tie-break's and the all-`y` one is not among them. The core it
;;; reports is the smallest union of a kept `(A k)` environment with `(B k)`'s,
;;; ten facts. The user ruled on 2026-11-05 (Q-M1e2.16) that the core search
;;; keeps its budget and **says the core was cut**; the exact core past the
;;; budget is F22's. So the right answer is that core, qualified as cut.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered, and what holds since ─────────────────────
;;;
;;; Until S1e2.2.23, at `e2a3263e` (S1e2.2.21's search, S1e2.2.22's parser),
;;; release and debug: R empty, exit 0, and root's core `(x1 k) (x2 k)
;;; (y1 k) … (y8 k)`, ten facts, refuted by `clash`, with nothing to say the
;;; search was cut, on every surface that prints it: the read-out's `unsat
;;; core` rows, `--json-summary`'s `region.core`, `--dump-answer`'s
;;; `nogoods.json`, `--dump-lattice`'s `nodes.json` and `nodes.md`,
;;; `--events`' `enter` line, `--trace`'s N, and `ein oracle --dump`'s
;;; `region.json` and `region.md` and `ein render region` drawing it. The
;;; search knew it was cut (`explain::Explanation::exhausted` was false), and
;;; `region.rs` dropped it. Since S1e2.2.23's fix the same ten facts are
;;; printed, and every surface says the search was cut at its 64 environments
;;; per fact: the read-out's `core search` row, *cut at its budget of 64
;;; environments per fact: a smaller core may exist*, and `core_status:
;;; "cut-environments"` beside the core in every JSON, in either build.

(relation x1 T) (relation y1 T) (relation p1 T) (relation x2 T) (relation y2 T) (relation p2 T) (relation x3 T) (relation y3 T) (relation p3 T) (relation x4 T) (relation y4 T) (relation p4 T) (relation x5 T) (relation y5 T) (relation p5 T) (relation x6 T) (relation y6 T) (relation p6 T) (relation x7 T) (relation y7 T) (relation p7 T) (relation x8 T) (relation y8 T) (relation p8 T) (relation A T) (relation B T)
(x1 k) (y1 k) (x2 k) (y2 k) (x3 k) (y3 k) (x4 k) (y4 k) (x5 k) (y5 k) (x6 k) (y6 k) (x7 k) (y7 k) (x8 k) (y8 k)
(rule lift (?X ?P) :match (?X ?v) :assert (?P ?v))
(lift x1 p1) (lift y1 p1) (lift x2 p2) (lift y2 p2) (lift x3 p3) (lift y3 p3) (lift x4 p4) (lift y4 p4) (lift x5 p5) (lift y5 p5) (lift x6 p6) (lift y6 p6) (lift x7 p7) (lift y7 p7) (lift x8 p8) (lift y8 p8)
(rule mk-a () :match (and (p1 ?v) (p2 ?v) (p3 ?v) (p4 ?v) (p5 ?v) (p6 ?v) (p7 ?v) (p8 ?v)) :assert (A ?v))
(rule mk-b () :match (and (y1 ?v) (y2 ?v) (y3 ?v) (y4 ?v) (y5 ?v) (y6 ?v) (y7 ?v) (y8 ?v)) :assert (B ?v))
(rule clash () :match (and (A ?v) (B ?v)) :assert (false))
